{{- /* Shared body for the modify_ JSON merge stubs: deep-merges a rendered
       managed document (.managed) over the target's current contents
       (.stdin), so apps that mix mutable state into their config files keep
       that state across applies. Managed keys always win -- including false
       and empty values (verified against this chezmoi build), which is why
       state-like keys must be OMITTED from managed documents, never left in
       as empty placeholders. Arrays replace wholesale; nested maps merge.
       Removing a key from a managed doc does not remove it from live files
       (install-only, the same contract as the package lists) -- removal is a
       one-time manual edit per machine. The live side is parsed with
       fromJsonc, not fromJson: VS Code and Windows Terminal treat their
       settings files as JSONC and this repo's live copies carry trailing
       commas in practice -- but comments do not survive a merge rewrite,
       since the output is re-serialized as strict pretty JSON. */ -}}
{{- $state := dict -}}
{{- with trim .stdin -}}
{{-   $state = fromJsonc . -}}
{{- end -}}
{{- mergeOverwrite $state .managed | toPrettyJson }}
